## Findings and fixes (all in 6718f72a5)

- F310 [Nit] FIX. Cause: the F282 landscape row reached only `WeekTileLinks`; the week
  page tile list in `page.tsx` kept a column, so the third tile ended at 462 px in the
  390 px viewport. Fix: the `data-week-tiles` list uses the same
  `[@media(max-height:500px)]` row with `flex-1` items; portrait and laptop keep the
  column. Fail-first: `landscape_controls_visible_week=false (control_bottom_px=462,
  controls_found=3, viewport_px=390)` on the old layout — the same 462 px the UX shot
  shows. After: `control_bottom_px=226`.
- F320 [Nit] FIX. The gate gains `controlRightAtLandscape`, four `landscape_row_right_edge`
  rows (end-of-book and week page rows, `th` and `en`, at 844x390), and a `/wide-row`
  self-test that the same function must reject. Measured on the old code: end-of-book th
  686, en 686; week th 686, en 686 — all at or below 844, so the English row does not
  overflow the viewport and no item change was needed (per the finding, the measured right
  edges are recorded instead). Self-test fail-first: the wide-row page is rejected with
  `control_right_px=1020 > viewport_width_px=844`.
- F290 [Nit] FIX (choice stated). I added the landscape orientation condition to the query
  — `[@media(max-height:500px)_and_(orientation:landscape)]:h-44!` and the matching
  `w-auto!` — and reworded the comment, instead of only rewording, because the cap exists
  for the landscape phone and the query then matches its stated purpose. The compiled CSS
  holds `@media (max-height:500px) and (orientation:landscape)`; a short desktop window
  and a portrait phone with a soft keyboard keep the full-size box. Every AC-8.2 row and
  the landscape rows stayed green, so the condition met its gate requirement.
- No song picture or content file changed. No committed Red or adversarial assertion
  changed; the gate rows only add checks.

